Subject: argv: stop the OR scan before reading past ARGV_LAST
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

check_or's upward scan starts at which_p + 2 and tested that entry
before testing which_p + 1 for ARGV_LAST. For the last option in the
table (fstrm_replay's -r), which_p + 1 is ARGV_LAST and which_p + 2 is
one past the end of the array, so the scan read out of bounds. Found by
Fil-C in test_fstrm_replay.sh. Test the nearer entry first.

--- a/libmy/argv.c
+++ b/libmy/argv.c
@@ -1880,8 +1880,8 @@
   if (match_p == NULL) {
     /* NOTE: we assume that which_p is not pointing now to ARGV_LAST */
     for (arg_p = which_p + 2;
-	 arg_p->ar_short_arg != ARGV_LAST
-	 && (arg_p - 1)->ar_short_arg != ARGV_LAST;
+	 (arg_p - 1)->ar_short_arg != ARGV_LAST
+	 && arg_p->ar_short_arg != ARGV_LAST;
 	 arg_p += 2) {
       if ((arg_p - 1)->ar_short_arg != ARGV_OR
 	  && (arg_p - 1)->ar_short_arg != ARGV_XOR) {
